      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFollow-up to #47616. When a stop string completes mid-step under speculative decoding, the output drops the tokens after it, but the generation token stats still count them.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `vllm:generation_tokens`, the per-request generation token histogram and the logged generation throughput no longer count tokens trimmed past a stop string.\n- `mean_time_per_output_token` for those requests uses the kept token count.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew `test_stop_string_trim_updates_generation_token_stats` (6 tokens in one step, stop string completes at token 4):\n\n```\npytest tests/detokenizer/test_stop_string_while_stop_model_terminates.py\n  main:        2 failed (assert 6 == 4), 34 passed\n  this branch: 36 passed\npytest tests/detokenizer/test_check_stop_strings.py tests/detokenizer/test_min_tokens.py \\\n       tests/detokenizer/test_stop_string_while_stop_model_terminates.py\n  this branch: 48 passed\n```\n\nCPU only (macOS). Not run here: `tests/v1/engine/test_output_processor.py`, whose imports load xgrammar's native library, which crashes on this machine. No model eval: this changes metrics only, not outputs.\n\n## Details\n\n`process_outputs` records iteration stats from `new_token_ids` (step 1) before the detokenizer matches stop strings, so `_trim_surplus_tokens` dropped the tokens from the output after they were counted. It now subtracts the dropped tokens from the iteration and request stats.\n\nNot a duplicate: a search of open PRs and issues for this trimming path and the generation token stats found none. #47616 fixed `token_ids` and logprobs only.\n\nAI assistance was used for this change.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
